u</surname><given-names>O</given-names></name><name><surname>Mafiana</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Dapo</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><article-title>Malaria among pregnant women in Abeokuta, Nigeria</article-title><source>Tanzania Health Research Bulletin</source><year>2006</year><volume>8</volume><fpage>28</fpage><lpage>31</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17058797</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B24"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><name><surname>Lamina</surname><given-names>MA</given-names></name><article-title>Gestational age sat first antenatal attendance in Sagamu, western Nigeria</article-title><source>Nig J Clin Pract</source><year>2004</year><volume>7</volume><issue>1</issue><fpage>1</fpage><lpage>3</lpage></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B25"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><name><surname>Sule-Odu</surname><given-names>AO</given-names></name><article-title>Maternal deaths in Sagamu, Nigeria</article-title><source>Int J Gynecol Obstet</source><year>2000</year><volume>69</volume><fpage>47</fpage><lpage>9</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0020-7292(99)00199-X</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B26"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><name><surname>Turkur</surname><given-names>IU</given-names></name><name><surname>Thatcher</surname><given-names>TD</given-names></name><name><surname>Sagay</surname><given-names>SA</given-names></name><name><surname>Madaki</surname><given-names>JKA</given-names></name><article-title>A comparison of sufadoxine-pyrimethamine with chloroquine and pyrimathaminefor prevention of malaria in pregnant Nigerian women</article-title><source>Am J Trop Med Hyg</source><year>2007</year><volume>76</volume><issue>6</issue><fpage>1019</fpage><lpage>1023</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17556604</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B27"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><name><surname>Anders</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><